==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|Swiss Standard German}} {{l/de|stossen}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|stozan|stōzan|lang=goh}} from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|stautaną|lang=gem-pro}}. Akin to Old Norse {{term|stauta|lang=non}} and {{term|steyta|lang=non}} (whence Danish {{term|støde|lang=da}}), Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌿𐍄𐌰𐌽|tr=stautan|lang=got}}. Non-Germanic cognates include Latin {{term|tundo|lang=la}}. Compare Sanskrit {{term|तुदति||tr=tudati|to strike, goad|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃtoːsən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-stoßen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=7|stößt|stieß|gestoßen}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=de}} to [[push]]; to [[shove]]; to [[thrust]]
# {{context|transitive|or|reflexive|lang=de}} to [[bump]]; to [[knock]]; to [[strike]]; to [[hurt]]
# {{context|reflexive|figuratively|with ''[[an#German|an]]''|lang=de}} to [[take exception]] (to something)
# {{context|intransitive|lang=de}} to [[jolt]]; to [[kick]]; to [[thrust]]

